since no man's sky launch for PC on  August 12 players have reported a myriad  of issues including crashes corrupt  saves and getting stuck under worlds  well good news space explorers hello  games has detailed the patches they've  released that address around seventy  percent of the current reported issues  details of the three patches for PC were  published on the game steam community  page patch one was focused on adding  greater support for hardware to maximize  the amount of people who are able to  experience the game this patch include  AMD phenom support mouse smoothing which  is helpful for players with sub 30  frames per second performance a fix for  frame stuttering due to the maximum FPS  cap and a solution to prevent safe  corruption patch to aim to increase  stability by addressing the most player  reported bugs and crashes the major  issue addressed in this patch was a  solution for players who found  themselves stuck under a world after  being shot down in a planet's atmosphere  this will no longer occur and if you are  currently stuck in subterranean  purgatory the game will detect this and  do its best to rescue you there've also  been fixes to crashes after warping  crashing while scanning crashing after  warping to a battle and winding up  inside a freighter and the game failing  to save until you died patch 3 targeted  the most common support requests while  also attempting to help players who have  become stranded or have corrupted save  files players who found themselves  stranded in a space station with a  busted ship and without the required  resources to repair it should find this  issue remedied along with the ability to  hopefully load corrupted saves fixes for  the three most reported issues the game  crashing due to a large amount of  discoveries a possible crash when a  player would collect a large number of  blueprints in a specific order and a  crash on the galactic map that would  occur if a player had set a large number  of waypoints have also been addressed  hello games has reiterated they will get  to work on new no man's sky features as  soon as the current issues with the pc  version have been fixed they wanted to  say that they expect to release at least  one major update next week no man's sky  director Sean Murray announced prior to  the game's launch that the ability to  build bases and own giant space Raiders  will be added to the game in the future  he has also revealed in an interview  with The Daily Star that suggesting the  game would only receive free updates  after launch was perhaps a little naive  are you interested to see what this  week's update brings to the game and how  are you finding the game aside from its  performance let me know in the comments  or find me on Twitter and for everything  you need to know about Daft Punk Jim  Henson puppets and restrictive inventory  systems keep coming by gamespot
 

